9T16:54:35Z"},"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-05-04T06:29:10Z","updated_at":"2026-05-18T16:09:56Z","closed_at":"2026-05-18T16:09:56Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: v4.7.dev3.official [60fff00a6], v4.7.beta1.official [1c8cc9e7e]\n- Not reproducible in: v4.6.2.stable.official [71f334935], v4.7.dev2.official [778cf54da]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.beta1 - CachyOS Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT Fri, 01 May 2026 19:46:26 +0000 on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Laptop GPU - AMD Ryzen 7 7735HS with Radeon Graphics (16 threads) - 14.86 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nSince v4.7.dev3 the following errors often appear in the output log when a new window is created (e.g. when a tooltip shows up or a dropdown is opened, may happen right on editor start):\n\n```\n  ERROR: drivers/vulkan/rendering_device_driver_vulkan.cpp:3465 - Condition \"err != VK_SUCCESS\" is true. Returning: false\n  ERROR: Surface did not return any valid formats.\n```\n\nLine numbers for v4.7.beta1, but error and method of triggering it are the same since v4.7.dev3.\n\nThis appears to be somewhat related to #117519, but this concerns a specific regression in 4.7 series instead of a broader issue (I haven't seen) that apparently also affects X11.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Enable \"Prefer Wayland\" in editor settings\n2. Create new windows in one way or another, e.g. by opening the main menu and quickly hovering over the options\n3. Observe errors in the output panel\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A, reproducible on a new project.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":1748